GABRIEL DAEMON PATCH — Fix health alert serialization bug
===========================================================
Author: Claude (co-architect for Robert Stephen Plowman)
Date: 2026-04-03

PROBLEM:
  memSet() uses String(value) on line 308, which converts JavaScript objects
  to "[object Object]" instead of proper JSON. This corrupts all health alerts
  and any other memcell values that are objects.

FIX:
  Replace String(value) with a smart serializer that JSON.stringifies objects
  and leaves strings/numbers alone.

  Line 307-308 — CHANGE FROM:
    db.prepare(`INSERT OR REPLACE INTO memcell (key, value, category, updated_at)
                VALUES (?, ?, ?, datetime('now'))`).run(key, String(value), category);

  TO:
    const serialized = (typeof value === 'object' && value !== null) ? JSON.stringify(value) : String(value);
    db.prepare(`INSERT OR REPLACE INTO memcell (key, value, category, updated_at)
                VALUES (?, ?, ?, datetime('now'))`).run(key, serialized, category);

  Line 310 — CHANGE FROM:
    memStore.set(key, { value, category, updated_at: new Date().toISOString() });

  TO:
    const fallbackVal = (typeof value === 'object' && value !== null) ? JSON.stringify(value) : String(value);
    memStore.set(key, { value: fallbackVal, category, updated_at: new Date().toISOString() });

ALSO FIX — HTTP memcell endpoint (around line 678):
  The POST /memcell/:key handler passes body.value directly to memSet.
  If body.value is an object (e.g. from JSON body), memSet should handle it.
  The fix above in memSet covers this case.

VERIFICATION:
  After applying fix, restart gabriel-daemon and test:
    curl -X POST http://localhost:7777/memcell/test:alert \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"value": {"severity": "warn", "msg": "test"}, "category": "health"}'
    
    curl http://localhost:7777/memcell/test:alert
    # Should return: {"key":"test:alert","value":"{\"severity\":\"warn\",\"msg\":\"test\"}","category":"health",...}
    # NOT: {"key":"test:alert","value":"[object Object]",...}
